# Day 60 

**33km / 11.5 hours**

*Moturimu Shelter to Makahika OPC*

Woke up feeling a bit sick. Nothing too bad, just a sore throat and a dour mood. The section ahead was marked 15km and 6-7 hours which was a bit puzzling since that's very slow but there was nothing for it but to get going and see how it goes. 

![The track ahead](./track.avif)

After the first 3km which were fairly gentle the proper track began and it became clear why the time estimate was quite high - it was steep, muddy and generally a slog to get through. It didn't take 6 hours but even the 4.5 or so hours it took to get to the hut was plenty difficult. There were some mountain bikers coming the other way which was pretty impressive given how the track was difficult on foot.

![Some baby geese wandering the road looking a bit confused](./goslings.avif)

After that there was a road where I put my head down and walked except I ended up going too far and missing the turnoff onto the track so had to backtrack a little. Oops. Then the track was quite tricky similar to the first one, also steep and tough going to get uphill. My legs were really feeling it and I also was feeling weary and dehydrated from the sweating throughout the day.

![The view from one of the lookouts](./lookout-view.avif)

There were some interesting lookouts after getting near the top of this section before a steep but consistent descent before heaps of stream crossings as it criss-crossed over and over. Then there was the campsite which was very minimal with the stream as the only water option and not much there so we soldiered on to another camping spot down the road which should make the next day a little easier.

![Just one of the many many streams to cross today](./stream.avif)
